---
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CampusExplorer from '../../../components/CampusExplorer.astro';
import CampusReferences from '../../../components/CampusReferences.astro';
import CampusAbbreviations from '../../../components/CampusAbbreviations.astro';
import 'katex/dist/katex.min.css';
import '../../../styles/data-analysis.css';
import '../../../styles/campus-safety.css';
const entry = (await getCollection('archive')).find(e=>e.data.slug==='campus-safety')!;
const {Content} = await render(entry);
const base='/data-analysis/campus-safety';
const data=JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}/data/dataset.json`,'utf8'));
const cases=JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}/data/case_study.json`,'utf8'));
const periods=[2022,2023,2024,'pooled'];
const n=(v:number)=>v.toLocaleString('en-US');
const example=(unitid:string,period:number|string)=>cases.find((r:any)=>r.unitid===unitid&&r.period===period);
---
<BaseLayout title={entry.data.title} description={entry.data.description} pageType="article" publishedTime="2026-09-25">
  <CampusAbbreviations institutions={data.institutions}><CampusReferences>
  <div class="analysis-page campus-study" data-campus-study>
    <header class="analysis-intro">
      <nav class="analysis-back" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/writing/">Writing</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/writing/data-analysis/">Data Analysis</a></nav>
      <p class="analysis-kicker">Campus safety data analysis · 25 September 2026</p>
      <h1>Campus safety,<br />in proportion.</h1>
      <p class="analysis-deck">Campus-housing offenses per 1,000 documented residents, with housing populations available for all ten University of California institutions and San Diego State. A broader enrollment-based view covers 42 universities, including the Ivy League.</p>
      <div class="analysis-actions"><a class="analysis-button" href="#explorer">Explore housing reports</a><a href="#methods">Read the methodology</a><a href={`${base}/downloads/campus-safety-report.pdf`}>Comprehensive report · PDF</a></div>
    </header>
    <section class="campus-summary" aria-labelledby="campus-summary-heading">
      <div><h2 id="campus-summary-heading">Campus housing, measured against residents.</h2><p>The opening view compares residential-facility reports with documented fall student-housing occupancy. Differences in reporting, property boundaries and who appears in the records still affect the comparison.</p><p>The explorer starts with <strong>2024 housing offenses per 1,000 documented residents</strong> at 11 institutions. Resident populations are unavailable for the other 31 institutions in the broader comparison set. Enrollment-based measures remain available for the broader comparison. Every displayed rate includes its count and population.</p></div>
      <div class="campus-facts"><div><strong>11</strong><span>institutions with documented housing occupancy <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.auditor.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2024-111-Report.pdf#page=62">State Auditor, Tables A.1–A.2</a></span></div><div><strong>42</strong><span>institutions in the broader comparison set <a data-campus-citation href={`${base}/data/PROTOCOL.md`}>Study protocol</a></span></div><div><strong>2022–24</strong><span>calendar report years <a data-campus-citation href="https://ope.ed.gov/campussafety/api/dataFiles/file?fileName=Crime2025EXCEL.zip">2025 federal collection</a></span></div><div><strong>15</strong><span>category views, including separate VAWA measures <a data-campus-citation href={`${base}/data/category_dictionary.csv`}>Category dictionary</a></span></div></div>
    </section>
    <aside class="analysis-notice"><strong>Interpretation.</strong> These are administrative reports, not convictions, unique victims or a student's probability of experiencing crime. Housing rates use fall occupancy with incompletely matched property boundaries. The study does not assign safety rankings. <a href="#methods">Definitions and limitations</a>.</aside>
    <nav class="analysis-section-nav" aria-label="Study sections"><a href="#explorer">Rate explorer</a><a href="#case-study">Housing comparison</a><a href="#source-notes">Source discrepancies</a><a href="#methods">Methods &amp; related research</a><a href="#downloads">Data &amp; audits</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
    <p class="analysis-note campus-explorer-sources">Explorer sources: reported counts from the 2025 federal collection <a data-campus-citation href="https://ope.ed.gov/campussafety/api/dataFiles/file?fileName=Crime2025EXCEL.zip">Federal bulk data</a>; documented housing occupancy from the California State Auditor <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.auditor.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2024-111-Report.pdf#page=62">State Auditor occupancy tables</a>; fall enrollment for the optional broader comparison from IPEDS <a data-campus-citation href="https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/use-the-data/download-access-database">IPEDS enrollment files</a>. Counts, populations and institution-specific notes are preserved in the published dataset <a data-campus-citation href={`${base}/data/dataset.json`}>Published dataset</a>.</p>
    <p class="analysis-note">Select a column heading to sort; select it again to reverse the order. Abbreviations are written out on first use. Hover over or focus an abbreviation for its full name or definition. <a data-campus-citation href={`${base}/data/PRESENTATION_REVISION.md`}>Abbreviation definitions and sources</a>.</p>
    <CampusExplorer data={data} />
    <section id="case-study" class="analysis-section" aria-labelledby="campus-case-heading">
      <div class="analysis-section-title"><span>02</span><div><h2 id="campus-case-heading">Housing reports: the time window matters</h2><p>A worked comparison from the originating UC and San Diego State research.</p></div></div>
      <p>The 2025 institutional security reports give <strong>20</strong> residential-facility rape offenses at UC San Diego <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf#page=142">UCSD 2025 ASR, p. 142</a> and <strong>1</strong> at SDSU's main campus for report year 2024 <a data-campus-citation href="https://police.sdsu.edu/_resources/files/annual-security-reports/2025-annual-security-report-finalized-08-18-25.pdf#page=7">SDSU 2025 ASR, p. 7</a>. Against documented fall housing occupancy <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.auditor.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2024-111-Report.pdf#page=62">State Auditor, Tables A.1–A.2</a>, that is <strong>0.91</strong> and <strong>0.12 per 1,000 residents</strong>. Across 2022–2024, the pooled ratios are much closer: <strong>0.73</strong> and <strong>0.70</strong>.</p>
      <p class="analysis-note">This explicitly versioned ASR comparison uses the named main-campus housing tables, with State Auditor occupancy. It is separate from the explorer's all-branch federal aggregation; historical SDSU housing aggregation remains unavailable there. Property boundaries are not fully matched, and offenses need not involve resident students. These are approximate descriptive ratios, not victimization probabilities or evidence of equivalent safety.</p>
      <div class="analysis-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="UC San Diego and SDSU main-campus housing comparison"><table><caption>Residential-facility rape offenses / actual fall housing occupancy</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Report period</th><th scope="col">UC San Diego: count / population</th><th scope="col">Rate per 1,000</th><th scope="col">SDSU main: count / population</th><th scope="col">Rate per 1,000</th></tr></thead><tbody>{periods.map(period=>{const u=example('110680',period);const s=example('122409',period);return <tr><th scope="row">{period==='pooled'?'2022–2024 pooled':period}</th><td>{n(u.asr_housing_rape_count)} / {n(u.fall_occupancy_sum)}</td><td>{u.rate_per_1000.toFixed(2)}</td><td>{n(s.asr_housing_rape_count)} / {n(s.fall_occupancy_sum)}</td><td>{s.rate_per_1000.toFixed(2)}</td></tr>;})}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="analysis-note">Pooled denominators sum three fall snapshots, not unique people. Table sources: <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf#page=142">UCSD 2025 ASR, p. 142</a> <a data-campus-citation href="https://police.sdsu.edu/_resources/files/annual-security-reports/2025-annual-security-report-finalized-08-18-25.pdf#page=7">SDSU 2025 ASR, p. 7</a> <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.auditor.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2024-111-Report.pdf#page=62">State Auditor, Tables A.1–A.2</a>. <a data-citation-exempt href={`${base}/data/asr_housing_case_study.csv`}>Download the calculation</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="source-notes" class="analysis-section" aria-labelledby="campus-source-heading">
      <div class="analysis-section-title"><span>03</span><div><h2 id="campus-source-heading">Source details that change interpretation</h2><p>Documented discrepancies and counting conventions remain visible in the results.</p></div></div>
      <div class="campus-case-grid">
        <article><h3>One disclosure can contain many offenses</h3><p>UC Santa Cruz's 2025 report explains that <strong>21 of its 38 residential rape offenses reported in 2024</strong> were disclosed in a single report. The published offense count is retained. It cannot be relabeled as 38 people or 38 report forms. <a data-campus-citation href="https://bpb-us-w2.wpmucdn.com/wordpress.ucsc.edu/dist/d/120/files/2025/09/2025-UC-Santa-Cruz-ASFSR_online-3.pdf#page=12">UCSC report, printed p. 11, footnote 6</a></p></article>
        <article><h3>Federal and campus tables can differ</h3><p>UCSD's 2022 on-campus rape count is <strong>14 in the frozen federal file</strong> and <strong>15 in its 2025 ASR</strong>; the noncampus count is 4 versus 5. The federal values remain in the explorer. A separate check of 36 rape cells across UCSD, UCSC and SDSU main found these two differences. <a data-campus-citation href={`${base}/data/asr_federal_rape_comparison.csv`}>Inspect all 36 source-cell comparisons</a> <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.police.ucsd.edu/docs/annualclery.pdf#page=142">UCSD 2025 ASR, p. 142</a> <a data-campus-citation href="https://ope.ed.gov/campussafety/api/dataFiles/file?fileName=Crime2025EXCEL.zip">2025 federal collection</a></p></article>
        <article><h3>Enrollment definitions require consistency</h3><p>For fall 2024, IPEDS reports <strong>41,137 students at SDSU</strong>; its Common Data Set and the State Auditor use <strong>39,373</strong>. The full population difference remains unresolved. The enrollment explorer uses IPEDS consistently across all institutions and years. <a data-campus-citation href={`${base}/data/DENOMINATORS.md`}>Review the denominator reconciliation</a> <a data-campus-citation href="https://asir.sdsu.edu/Documents/CommonDataSets/CDS_2024-25.pdf#page=3">SDSU Common Data Set, p. 3</a> <a data-campus-citation href="https://www.auditor.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2024-111-Report.pdf#page=62">State Auditor, Tables A.1–A.2</a></p></article>
        <article><h3>Missing coverage is not a zero</h3><p>All 42 institutions have complete 2024 on-campus counts. Earlier source-year gaps prevent complete pooled totals for six institutions. Housing applicability is documented separately: current no-housing declarations are used for 2024 only, without backfilling earlier years. <a data-campus-citation href={`${base}/data/COVERAGE.md`}>Review coverage and applicability rules</a></p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="methods" class="analysis-section" aria-labelledby="campus-methods-heading">
      <div class="analysis-section-title"><span>04</span><div><h2 id="campus-methods-heading">Methods and related research</h2><p>Definitions, formulas, source alignment and interpretive limits.</p></div></div>
      <article class="analysis-prose"><Content /></article>
    </section>
    <section id="downloads" class="analysis-section" aria-labelledby="campus-downloads-heading">
      <div class="analysis-section-title"><span>05</span><div><h2 id="campus-downloads-heading">Data, sources and audit record</h2><p>Inspect the inputs and calculations behind the website.</p></div></div>
      <div class="analysis-downloads"><a href={`${base}/downloads/campus-safety-report.pdf`}><strong>Comprehensive research report</strong><span>Original report covering resident and enrollment measures · PDF</span></a><a href={`${base}/downloads/campus-safety-reproducibility.zip`}><strong>Reproducibility package</strong><span>Aggregate source extracts, code, rates and audit records · ZIP</span></a><a href={`${base}/data/annual_rates.csv`}><strong>Annual rates</strong><span>All categories and population measures · CSV</span></a><a href={`${base}/data/pooled_rates.csv`}><strong>Pooled 2022–2024 rates</strong><span>Counts, summed populations and availability · CSV</span></a><a href={`${base}/data/source_manifest.json`}><strong>Source manifest</strong><span>URLs, versions, retrieval dates and original-file hashes · JSON</span></a><a href={`${base}/data/artifact_manifest.json`}><strong>Published artifact manifest</strong><span>File sizes and SHA-256 checksums · JSON</span></a></div>
      <div class="campus-audits"><article><h3>Calculations and data</h3><p>Independent source joins, arithmetic, pooled denominators, missingness and category reconciliation.</p><a href={`${base}/data/INDEPENDENT_NUMERICAL_AUDIT.md`}>Read the numerical audit</a></article><article><h3>Methods and presentation</h3><p>Comparable primary research, mathematical notation and responsive website/PDF checks.</p><a href={`${base}/data/RESEARCH_REVIEW.md`}>Related research</a> · <a href={`${base}/data/VISUAL_AUDIT.md`}>Visual audit</a></article><article><h3>Sources and citations</h3><p>A separate claim-by-claim audit of source support, locators and qualification.</p><a href={`${base}/data/CITATION_AUDIT.md`}>Read the citation audit</a></article></div>
      <p class="analysis-note">This study reports documented administrative measures. It is not externally peer reviewed, and source verification does not establish complete reporting or matched personal exposure. Study snapshot: 25 September 2026.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  </CampusReferences></CampusAbbreviations>
</BaseLayout>
